From: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: sm8150-xiaomi-raphael: wide IMX586 node on CCI0 master0

The wide module answers at **0x1a on CCI0 master0** (measured, see
evidence/raw/camera-cci-probe-rounds14-19.txt), not at the address the stock DT
implies.  Its rails are viodd (1.8 V), BOB (3.008-4.0 V), S8 through the
CAMW_VDIG_EN pad (gpio90), plus the PM8150 SMPS5 (2.0 V) and LDO17 (3.1 V) rails
that only this module needs, its MCLK is MCLK0 (gpio13), reset is gpio28 and the
CSI side is CSIPHY0.

The driver imported in camera/drivers/imx586.c looks its supplies up by the
uppercase names VANA/VDIG/VDDL, so the node uses exactly those property names.
No `regulator-always-on` anywhere: the sensors stay unpowered until a driver or a
test asks for them (two boot bricks came from forcing PMIC rail flags).

Not tested yet - written while the phone was wedged (round 22).

Signed-off-by: Winter21c <winter@localhost>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8150-xiaomi-raphael.dts
@@ 	cci: cci@ac4a000 {
 		i2c-bus@0 {
 			reg = <0>;
 			clock-frequency = <400000>;
+
+			/* wide camera: IMX586, CSIPHY0, MCLK0 gpio13,
+			 * reset gpio28, VDIG_EN gpio90 */
+			imx586_wide: camera@1a {
+				compatible = "sony,imx586";
+				reg = <0x1a>;
+				reset-gpios = <&tlmm 28 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+				clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_MCLK0_CLK>;
+				clock-names = "xvclk";
+				assigned-clocks = <&camcc CAM_CC_MCLK0_CLK>;
+				assigned-clock-rates = <24000000>;
+
+				/* names match camera/drivers/imx586.c */
+				VANA-supply = <&vreg_bob>;
+				VDIG-supply = <&camera_vdig_wide>;
+				VDDL-supply = <&camera_viodd_ldo>;
+				vs5-supply = <&vreg_s5a_2p0>;
+				vl17-supply = <&vreg_l17a_3p0>;
+
+				status = "okay";
+
+				port {
+					imx586_wide_ep: endpoint {
+						link-frequencies = /bits/ 64 <1800000000 900000000>;
+						data-lanes = <0 1 2 3>;
+						remote-endpoint = <&csiphy0_ep>;
+					};
+				};
+			};
 		};
